**Changes made:** Fixed a single lint issue in the existing `cmd/ts/main.go` — the `fmt.Fprintf` return value on the output write was unchecked (`errcheck`). Replaced the bare `fmt.Fprintf(os.Stdout, ...)` with a `bufio.NewWriter(os.Stdout)` pattern (per design decision D3) that checks write and flush errors, breaking out of the loop on failure. This aligns with both the Go style constitution's error handling rules and the design decision to use buffered output with per-line flushing (R1.3).